    {
        "content": "<p>If the types are the same only in an <code>implicit_reducible</code> way, it doesn't make sense to ask that some instances are the same at <code>instance_reducible</code> transparency, because already the types are not transparent enough for this.</p>\n<p>I guess this is an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XY_problem\">#xy</a> problem: why would you like to have that?</p>",
        "id": 623119091,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1789040050
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The motivation is in <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"376152\">@Paul Lezeau</span> 's project of formalization of statement of Hodge conjecture I needed to resolve the following example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instance_reducible</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Sheaf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instCategorySheaf</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">aux_1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instCategorySheaf</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">aux_3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TopCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instCategorySheaf</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">aux_5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Over</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">CommRingCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instCategorySheaf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGrpCat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TopCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ComplexPoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ObjectProperty</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FullSubcategory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">category</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Presheaf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsSheaf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Opens</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">grothendieckTopology</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ComplexPoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible_and_instances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 623119506,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1789040163
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But why would you need the equality <code>with_reducible_and_instances rfl</code>? Normally this is never relevant, what matters is <code>with_implicit</code>.</p>",
        "id": 623121113,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1789040623
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah in my application with implicit is enough but I still wanna know if it's possible to have different reducible setting with <code>def Y := X deriving blah</code></p>",
        "id": 623137599,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1789044330
    }
]